    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d701">

                <pb facs="0704" n="604" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6983: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-11T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>72. For Admiral McCully.</p>
                <p>Your 55, June 1st.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d701-f1"/> Is Department to understand
                    that Wrangel’s negotiations with Soviets, proposed by British, look to mere
                    armistice with continuation Wrangel’s control of Crimea, or extension of Soviet
                    rule over Crimea with amnesty to Wrangel’s forces?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
